<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Siamese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893</span> · Also known as Franco-Siamese crisis of 1893</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Siamese War was a brief conflict in 1893 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Kingdom of Siam over the Lao lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a>. After French gunboats forced their way up the Chao Phraya to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paknam-incident">Paknam incident</a> in July, Siam accepted a treaty in October ceding the territory east of the Mekong, which France organised as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-siamese-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Siamese War" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Nash · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Franco-Siamese_Frontier_Dispute,_the_French_forcing_the_Menam_-_The_Graphic_-_1893.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
